 "notes": "ADMX Run 1C 90% C.L. upper limit on g_agamma over 800-1020 MHz (3.3-4.2 ueV), Fig. 4 (run1c_sensitivity.png from the e-print, 4800x3000 px). Digitised the lower boundary of the dark-red 'Maxwellian' region (boosted Maxwell-Boltzmann, rho=0.45 GeV/cc), the paper's main scenario; the light-pink 'N-body' curve (rho=0.6 GeV/cc) was not used. No density rescaling needed since 0.45 GeV/cc is the canonical value. Axes calibrated from tick marks (x: 650/750/850/950 MHz majors, 10.082 px/MHz; y: log scale, 1e-15 at row 1198, 1874 px/decade, minor ticks 2e-16..2e-15 fit to <0.5 px). Calibration cross-checked against the KSVZ/DFSZ dashed lines (g=alpha*g_gamma/pi/f_a with m_a=6.2 ueV x 1e12 GeV/f_a), agreeing to ~1%. Each of the 109 points is the median boundary over a ~2 MHz bin, so narrow deep spikes and RFI notches are smoothed; the jagged fine structure of the true limit deviates locally from these medians. Consistent with the paper's statements: KSVZ excluded over 3.3-4.2 ueV, DFSZ over 3.9-4.1 ueV.",
